<title>UK: Stagecoach says in rail franchise shortlist.</title>
<headline>Stagecoach says in rail franchise shortlist.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British transport group Stagecoach Holdings Plc said on Thursday it had been shortlisted to operate the franchises of four U.K. passenger rail lines.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it had been shortlisted to operate for Central Trains Ltd, Intercity West Coast Ltd, North West Regional Railways Ltd and Scotrail Railways Ltd.</p>
<p>Britain is about halfway through the privatisation, by franchise contract, of 25 train operating companies and a number of firms shortlisted for the latest batch under consideration have announced they have been shortlisted in recent weeks.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717</p>
